      "previewText": "Gaseous radon-222 forms in soil. As it rises from the soil, it can be trapped in basements below homes. This gas, an alpha emitter, decays into Po-218; once inhaled by people, it can cause lung cancer. A sample of gas is tested for Rn-222. The half-life of Rn-222 is 3.823 days. After @@days@@ days, the sample is found to contain @@gramsRn@@×10–8 g of Rn-222. How many grams of Rn-222 were initially present?  gHow many grams of Po-218 have been formed? g",
      "targeted": [],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "children": [],
          "data": [
            {
              "children": [],
              "expression": "// Two variable definitions\nconst gramsRn = OLI.random(1.02,9.98,2) .toFixed(2);\nconst daysIndex = OLI.random(0,6);\nconst daysArray = [32,35,38,41,44,47,51,54,58,62,65]\nconst days = daysArray[daysIndex];\nconst initialRn = gramsRn*Math.exp(0.1813*days)/100000000;\nconst answer1 = initialRn .toPrecision(3);\nconst answer1low = answer1*0.97;\nconst answer1high = answer1*1.03;\nconst amountPo = initialRn*218/222;\nconst answer2 = amountPo .toPrecision(3);\nconst answer2low = answer2*0.97;\nconst answer2high = answer2*1.03;\n\n// Expose variables to OLI\nmodule.exports = {\n  gramsRn,\n  days,\n  initialRn,\n  answer1,\n  answer1low,\n  answer1high,\n  amountPo,\n  answer2,\n  answer2low,\n  answer2high\n};\n",
